[2026-09-18 20:05:04] REQ 260918200412-25 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=50 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_v28usuek","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"ABRT\\|fsm-state\\|gptel--fsm\\|aborted\" /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/tools/agent/delegate.el | head -20; echo \"=== how does completion hook know the turn was aborted? ===\"; grep -n \"ABRT\" /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/tools/agent/delegate.el"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:05:00] 174:c149 (2026-09-10, aria c148 failure): the old design aborted first and\n175:completed via a 1s fallback timer, assuming gptel-abort's ABRT\n187:entry guard skip the aborted request entirely.\"\n202:    ;; callback, completion hook's entry guard skips the ABRT).\n313:The hook is called at every gptel response boundary (DONE, ERRS, ABRT).\n442:                         (format \"Delegate '%s' FAILED (max text-only turns reached, reasoning-only: %d turns produced no content and no result marker; last turn's thinking was aborted by the thinking-loop guard).\"\n539:      ;; Completion hook: called by gptel at DONE, ERRS, or ABRT state.\n=== how does completion hook know the turn was aborted? ===\n175:completed via a 1s fallback timer, assuming gptel-abort's ABRT\n202:    ;; callback, completion hook's entry guard skips the ABRT).\n313:The hook is called at every gptel response boundary (DONE, ERRS, ABRT).\n539:      ;; Completion hook: called by gptel at DONE, ERRS, or ABRT state.\n\n[t+00:48/60:00 c22/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_hsuimv2y","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '530,570p' /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/tools/agent/delegate.el; echo \"=== does the hook fire on ABRT? check gptel fork ===\"; grep -n \"ABRT\" /root/i.ar/emacs.d/gptel-fork/gptel.el 2>/dev/null | head -10"}}}]},{"role":"tool","conten