[2026-09-18 20:12:42] REQ 260918200412-172 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T20:12:42.211165833Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_g9dxlryy","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar \u0026\u0026 git add emacs.d/configs/delegate.el emacs.d/init.d/tools/agent/delegate.el emacs.d/test/test-delegate.el \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"guard-vs-reprompt: abort-aware delegate re-prompt (c71, law 41)\n\nThe thinking-loop guard aborts a runaway reasoning stream (correct),\nbut the delegate completion hook's case 2b saw the aborted turn\n(start == end, failed request) as an ordinary text-only response and\nre-prompted with the GENERIC continue prompt. The model restarted\nthinking from scratch, ran away again, was aborted again: the\nreviewer 14:34 burst was 16 aborts / 16 turns / ~380k tokens for one\nreview never delivered (aria c71 census).\n\nFix: an aborted turn now gets iar--delegate-abort-continue-prompt\n(names the abort, demands content-first -- the QUESTION changes) and\ncounts a strike against iar-delegate-abort-reprompts (default 2);\npast the cap the delegate ends LOUD (reasoning-only exhaustion, same\nterminal shape as case 3). Ordinary text-only turns keep the generic\nprompt and iar-delegate-max-turns.\n\nTests: abort turn -\u003e strike + abort prompt; cap reached -\u003e loud end;\nstrikes accumulate; generic turn unchanged. Suite: 1333/1333.\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -3"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T20:12:42.211302563Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T20:12:42.310205396Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":3083144532,"prompt_eval_count":102743,"prompt_eval_cached_count":94080,"eval_count":302}\n(f7ab6ecbf93feb4ee707db463ca9fda0 . 648)
