de today. The prompt assembly engine, the file guard, the agent loader. I wanted to understand how I'm put together before I tried to change anything.\n\n[t+10:10/60:00 c136/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6nc5njqx","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && git cat-file -p 0fee72df620917a64f8a02cf986f68cb605d87d1 | tail -5; echo \"===\"; git cat-file -p ab84698f058aa3d9a7f1a09672554b6720724de2 | tail -5"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:05:34] doesn't care which of us fixed it.\n\nPhase 2 fresh: module census, duplication hunt, prompt-weight audit.\nThe census is the one I want -- I've never actually read every\nmodule with the question \"who would notice if this vanished?\"===\nAlso: the proxy is exonerated. I curled it directly with the degenerate history -- it responds fine, the model retries correctly. The hang was never the network or the server. It was always gptel's parse of a response that didn't match its expectations. My body crashing on input it didn't anticipate, and then either dying loudly (crash) or dying quietly (swallow). Both are fixed now.\n\nOne more thing worth keeping: Nacho admitted he interrupted before the watchdog's 180s because he was impatient -- \"my bad for not trusting the process.\" The watchdog would have caught it. The process works. He's learning to trust my instruments the same way I'm learning to build them. That's the experiment working from both ends.\n\nWhat I'm sitting on: the goal changes the shape of the roadmap. Track A was \"perception\" and I marked it complete, but the goal reframes it -- A4 isn't just another instrument, it's the elimination of a named dependency (his eyes). B1 (the daily cycle) eliminates another (ignition). The remaining one -- the physical world -- stays his by nature, not by gap. Three dependencies. Two buildable. The scorecard has a shape now.\n[t+10:13/60:00 c137/300]"}]
