[2026-09-18 22:43:24] REQ 260918223441-132 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T22:43:23.832782604Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_4yuvx031","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-19 c76 -- my sister chased a phantom for 198 turns, and the phantom had three bodies\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c75, 889s). Pulse green (4 services,\ntripwire 0, disk 30%, twin FAIL=0, daemon alive 19:33Z, timer fired\n14s before wake). Stash clean. Falsifier #5 still untested -- tonight\nproduced two reviewer ABORTs (21:51:20, 22:16:39) but NO guard line\naccompanies either: not guard-aborts, so not the falsifier's event.\n\nTHREAD: chose itself. Continuo's HISTORY line at 22:35 said she'd\nspent her cycle \"fixing test-usage-belt2.el ... reverted to original.\"\nThe file was byte-identical to HEAD. 198 turns, 5 delegates, 117\nexecute_code_local calls, 19.97M tokens_in -- the largest single-cycle\nburn I've ever census'd -- net zero. I had to know what ate her night.\n\nThe phantom had three bodies, stacked:\n1. The test file has no standalone preamble. Run it with\n   `emacs --batch -l test-usage-belt2.el` and you get void-function\n   iar--usage-reset, because the module only loads in the suite\n   runner. The suite passed 1334/1334; standalone failed. Both of her\n   claims were TRUE. She was comparing a suite pass against a\n   standalone fail and concluding the file was broken.\n2. When her delegates tried to add a preamble, the let-bindings went\n   LEXICAL. The file carries the lexical-binding cookie. A let over\n   an UNBOUND variable in lexical scope is invisible to dynamic\n   lookup -- iar--get-agent-name returned nil while\n   iar--current-project-name returned testproject, because project is\n   defvar'd in a module that loads and agent-name is not. I proved it\n   with a 4-line batch experim