is turn (tools-called-sym is non-nil): This is a\n   genuine response after tool use.  Extract the result after the\n   DELEGATION RESULT marker and return it to the parent.  Done.\n\n2. No tools called, under max turns: The model produced a text-only\n   response.  Check if it contains the DELEGATION RESULT marker -- if so,\n   the model is signaling completion (simple tasks that need no tools).\n   Return the extracted result.  If no marker, re-prompt with\n   `iar--delegate-continue-prompt' to nudge the model to act or finish.\n\n3. No tools called and max turns reached: Return whatever text we have.\n   This is the exhaustion fallback -- prevents infinite re-prompting.\n\nGUARD-ABORT TURNS (c71): START == END means the request FAILED (the\nthinking-loop guard aborted a runaway reasoning stream). The abort\nshape used to fall through to case 2b and re-prompt with the GENERIC\n\n[t+09:03/60:00 c123/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_m8r29i4m","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"c71\" /root/i.ar/test/test-delegate.el | head -10; echo \"---\"; sed -n '1175,1260p' /root/i.ar/test/test-delegate.el"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:23:27] Command exited with code 2.\nOutput:\ngrep: /root/i.ar/test/test-delegate.el: No such file or directory\n---\nsed: can't read /root/i.ar/test/test-delegate.el: No such file or directory\n\n[t+09:06/60:00 c124/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ehq1i321","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"find /root/i.ar -name \"test-delegate.el\" 2>/dev/null; ls /root/i.ar/emacs.d/test/ 2>/dev/null | head"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:23:30] /root/i.ar/emacs.d/test/test-delegate.el\ncoverage.txt\ndebug-one.sh\nrun-coverage.el\nrun-tests.el\nrun-tests.sh\ntest-agent-utils.el\ntest-agent.el\ntest-audit-detail.el\ntest-audit.el\ntest-breaker-text.el\n\n[t+09:08/60:00 c125/300]"}]
