[2026-09-19 00:23:55] REQ 260919001422-130 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T00:23:55.31332129Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_rmcov8fx","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c 'PYEOF'\n# Plan the fix precisely.\n# Current cond order in iar--delegate-completion-fn:\n#   (cond\n#     (tools-called ...)                       ; Case 1 -- NO abort check\n#     ((and (not tools-called) has-marker)...) ; Case 2a\n#     ((\u003c turn-count max-turns) ...)           ; Case 2b incl. aborted-turn branch\n#     (t ...)                                  ; Case 3 exhaustion\n#\n# The bug: an ABORTED turn (start==end) with tools-called=t from a PRIOR turn's tool\n# execution lands in Case 1 and returns the raw buffer as \"completed\".\n#\n# Fix: hoist the aborted-turn check ABOVE the tools-called check. If start==end:\n#   - the request FAILED regardless of prior tool use this turn\n#   - route to the same strike/abort-aware logic (strike++, under cap -\u003e re-prompt\n#     with abort-aware prompt; past cap -\u003e end LOUD)\n# But CAREFUL: the aborted-turn branch currently lives inside the Case-2b arm\n# ((\u003c turn-count max-turns)). If I hoist abort detection to the top, I must\n# replicate the strike logic there. Cleanest: new FIRST cond arm:\n#   ((and (number-or-marker-p start) (number-or-marker-p end) (= start end))\n#    -\u003e aborted-turn handling: strike counting + abort-aware re-prompt or LOUD end)\n# and REMOVE the aborted-turn special-case from the 2b arm (it becomes dead code).\n#\n# Wait -- one subtlety. In the c79 reviewer case, the abort fired at the -170 turn.\n# tools-called was t (from -169). If I hoist abort detection first, the delegate\n# would: strike 1, re-prompt with abort-aware prompt. The reviewer would then\n# synthesize its final review with a changed question. That's the DESIGNED 